WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.030
- I also noticed though

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:03.980
you were really motivated
to get fit this year.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.370
I wish that'd happened to me,

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.010
but can we see the photos

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:09.140
to represent what I'm talking about?

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.283
What the hell?

00:00:11.283 --> 00:00:12.680
(Busta Rhymes laughs)

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:13.820
What are you doing?

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.740
Asking for a friend.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.630
- I think the beautiful thing in life

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:22.630
is the hill and the gully ride, you know?

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:23.623
- Yeah.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.760
- And I was really going through

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.760
probably one of my most
challenging times in my life.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.890
I've had some lows like we all go in,

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:37.650
none of us exempt from
actually going through

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.310
some sort of hardship,

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:43.923
but I lost my dad in, I believe, 2014,

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.700
and I didn't deal with it
in like a real mourning way.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.386
I kind of just drowned myself in work.

00:00:52.386 --> 00:00:53.219
- Yeah.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:56.810
- And I kinda really
neglected to take care of me.

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:59.423
I was at about 340 pounds.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:03.633
I was having issues with my health,

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:05.820
and wasn't telling anybody.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.930
I had blood, I was on
blood pressure medicine.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:12.190
I was on two blood pressure
medicines, by the way.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:15.090
I was on a acid reflux medicine,

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:18.810
and I also had a horrible sleep apnea,

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:23.640
and I was also growing
polyps on my throat.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.910
And it just reached an apex,

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:27.890
and it got to a point where,

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:30.750
you know, my son, my oldest son,

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.900
who I had working as my
role manager at the time,

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:38.720
was so disappointed at what he saw in me.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.510
And I never heard that from my son before.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.460
So it was a crossroads,

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:45.730
and I wasn't happy with
the way I was feeling

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:48.360
and the way I was looking at myself.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.220
And I knew in order to put this music out,

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:53.830
I needed to not just sound incredible,

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.330
but I needed to feel incredible,

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:56.870
and I needed to look incredible,

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:57.820
and I wanted to make sure

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:02.710
that I had successfully
executed doing everything

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:05.680
that I was able to do within my means

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:08.030
and within my control
and within my ability

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.670
to not leave a stone unturned

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:14.860
when it came to securing this win,

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:18.570
which is probably one of
my greatest wins ever.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:19.403
- Aw, that feels...

00:02:19.403 --> 00:02:20.940
That's gotta feel great, man.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.350
Like, I do know that feeling
when you work on something,

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:24.183
you're like, man,

00:02:24.183 --> 00:02:26.700
I don't even care how
it works out out there.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.250
It got out of me, I'm so
proud of it, I did it.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:31.740
That's gotta feel amazing, and.

